@inject LessonCatalog Catalog
@if (Section == "learn")
{
<section class="lesson-section"><div class="section-intro"><span class="eyebrow">BUILD THE MENTAL MODEL</span><h2>Small enough to understand. Real enough to explore.</h2><p>Learn the complete path from a Razor component to Claude and back.</p></div><div class="learning-grid">
@foreach (var item in Learning) { <article class="learning-card"><span class="eyebrow">@item.Label</span><h3>@item.Title</h3><p>@item.Text</p></article> }
</div><aside class="lesson-note"><strong>Know which SDK you are using.</strong><p>The official Anthropic C# SDK calls the Claude Messages API. The Claude Agent SDK supports Python and TypeScript and adds the CLI-backed agent loop. This native .NET edition demonstrates the same introductory one-prompt lesson with the C# client, no tools and no subprocess bridge.</p><a href="https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/cli-sdks-libraries/sdks/csharp" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the official C# SDK documentation ↗</a></aside><a class="lesson-button primary" href="/setup">Set up the application →</a></section>
}
else if (Section == "setup")
{
<section class="lesson-section"><div class="section-intro"><span class="eyebrow">WINDOWS TERMINAL · POWERSHELL</span><h2>One AppHost. Shared native and web UI.</h2><p>Use .NET 10, the Windows MAUI workload, WebView2 and the pinned Aspire packages. No Python or Node.js runtime is required.</p></div>
<article class="lesson-step"><h3>1. Restore this independent solution</h3><CodeBlock Code="@RestoreCommands" Language="powershell" /><p>The AppHost uses Aspire 13.6.4. MAUI hosting is an explicitly pinned preview integration. The native client targets Windows; Android/iOS/Mac packaging is outside this edition.</p></article>
<article class="lesson-step"><h3>2. Configure the Web API key</h3><CodeBlock Code="@EnvCommands" Language="powershell" /><CodeBlock Code="@EnvExample" Language="ini" Source="ROOT .ENV · API ONLY" /><p>Save your own key before starting. Only the API loads this file; it is never forwarded to MAUI, the browser host or the AppHost. Environment variables/user secrets override file values. Restart the API after changes. Max output tokens accept 1–8192.</p></article>
<article class="lesson-step"><h3>3. Start Aspire</h3><CodeBlock Code=".\Start-Application.ps1" Language="powershell" /><p>Open the dashboard login URL printed by Aspire. The browser companion is <a href="http://127.0.0.1:5000">http://127.0.0.1:5000</a>; Web API docs are <a href="http://127.0.0.1:8400/docs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">http://127.0.0.1:8400/docs</a>. The dashboard manages service lifecycles, logs, traces and discovery. Ctrl+C stops the AppHost and its managed processes.</p><p>The native Windows resource is explicit-start: launch it from the Aspire dashboard when ready. You can also use Start-Hybrid.ps1 while Aspire is running. The MAUI app uses a real BlazorWebView and shares the same Razor components, not a wrapper around the browser site.</p></article>
<article class="lesson-step"><h3>Verify and build</h3><CodeBlock Code="@VerifyCommands" Language="powershell" /><p>SDK tests replace the HTTP transport and need no credits. The browser companion supports inspecting the shared UI without launching a desktop window. Native Windows build checks are separate from native runtime testing.</p></article>
<aside class="lesson-note"><strong>Health means connectivity.</strong><p>A green indicator reports that the API can be reached. Key presence does not prove authentication, model access or billing readiness. Simple mode returns 503 without a key; Stream emits an error and closes. The typed client uses cancellation and does not automatically retry model POST requests.</p></aside><a class="lesson-button primary" href="/">Try Hello world! →</a></section>
}
else if (Section == "architecture")
{
<section class="lesson-section"><div class="section-intro"><span class="eyebrow">FOLLOW ONE REQUEST</span><h2>See how the pieces connect.</h2><p>MAUI Blazor Hybrid and the browser companion share a Razor UI. A typed C# client calls the separate Web API. Aspire handles orchestration, discovery and telemetry beside this request path. The official C# SDK streams Claude’s response as an async enumerable.</p></div><div class="architecture-flow" role="list">@foreach (var layer in Layers) { <div class="architecture-node" role="listitem"><span>@layer.Label</span><strong>@layer.Title</strong><p>@layer.Text</p></div> }</div>
<article class="lesson-step"><h3>Aspire connects the resources</h3><p>The AppHost starts the API and browser host, registers the native Windows target, injects service discovery and connects OpenTelemetry to its dashboard. No model key is put in client resource configuration.</p><CodeBlock Code="@Catalog.OrchestrationCode" Language="csharp" Source="src/SmallestAgent.AppHost/Program.cs" /></article><figure class="lesson-step uml-card"><span class="eyebrow">UML SEQUENCE DIAGRAM</span><h3>From a click to a final answer</h3><p>Read top to bottom. Dashed lines are lifelines. Solid arrows are calls; dashed arrows carry responses. Loop and alternative frames explain streaming, completion and errors.</p><div class="uml-viewport" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Scrollable UML sequence diagram"><img src="_content/SmallestAgent.Shared/workflow.svg" width="1440" height="1660" alt="16 numbered interactions linking the browser, MAUI/shared Razor component and typed C# client, ASP.NET Core endpoints, official C# SDK, and Claude API." /></div><figcaption>One Messages API turn. No tools. Private server configuration.</figcaption><div class="diagram-downloads"><a href="_content/SmallestAgent.Shared/workflow.svg" download>Download UML diagram (SVG)</a><a href="_content/SmallestAgent.Shared/workflow.puml" download>Download editable PlantUML source</a></div></figure>
<div class="section-intro"><h3>Follow every UML arrow in the code</h3><p>Each numbered card matches an arrow in the diagram. Excerpts below are generated directly from this application’s source. Surrounding context is omitted.</p></div>
@foreach (var step in Catalog.Steps) { <article class="lesson-step workflow-code-step" id="uml-step-@step.Number"><span class="step-number">@step.Number</span><h3>@step.Number. @step.Title</h3><p>@step.Text</p><CodeBlock Code="@step.Code" Language="@step.Language" Source="@step.Source" /><div class="workflow-code-explanation"><strong>How this code explains step @step.Number</strong><p>@step.Explanation</p></div></article> }
<aside class="lesson-note"><strong>Text streaming and completion are different.</strong><p>TextDelta carries a piece of text. ResultMessage contains the complete answer and usage. The done event closes transport; it does not turn a max_tokens stop into a successful full response. USD cost is not reported by the Messages API, so the UI does not invent it.</p></aside><a class="lesson-button primary" href="/walkthrough">Read the code walkthrough →</a></section>
}
else
{
<section class="lesson-section"><div class="section-intro"><span class="eyebrow">READ THE CODE · UNDERSTAND THE FLOW</span><h2>The same lesson. Native C#.</h2><p>Five source excerpts explain the application’s boundaries: input, HTTP, SDK iteration, result projection and safe rendering.</p></div>
@foreach (var number in new[] { 1, 2, 4, 10, 12 }) { var step = Catalog.Steps.Single(x => x.Number == number); <article class="lesson-step"><span class="eyebrow">SOURCE WALKTHROUGH</span><h3>@step.Title</h3><p>@step.Text</p><CodeBlock Code="@step.Code" Language="@step.Language" Source="@step.Source" /><p>@step.Explanation</p></article> }
<aside class="lesson-note"><strong>The central loop</strong><p>Build MessageCreateParams, call CreateStreaming and consume with await foreach. Everything around that loop makes the request understandable, validated and usable in a browser.</p></aside><a class="lesson-button primary" href="/">Watch it run →</a></section>
}
@code {
    [Parameter] public string Section { get; set; } = "learn";
    private const string RestoreCommands = "cd .\\09-smallest-agent-aspire-maui\ndotnet --version\ndotnet workload list\ndotnet restore SmallestAgent.slnx --configfile NuGet.Config";
    private const string EnvCommands = "if (!(Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item .env.example .env }\nnotepad .env";
    private const string EnvExample = "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_actual_api_key\nCLAUDE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5\nAGENT_MAX_TOKENS=1024\nAGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT=You are a helpful assistant. Answer clearly and concisely.";
    private const string VerifyCommands = "pwsh -File scripts/Generate-Lesson.ps1\ndotnet build SmallestAgent.slnx\ndotnet run --project tests/SmallestAgent.Checks";
    private static readonly (string Label, string Title, string Text)[] Learning = [
        ("01 / INTERFACE", "Build with Blazor", "Shared Razor components run in MAUI BlazorWebView and the interactive browser companion. A typed C# client handles HTTP streaming."),
        ("02 / REQUEST", "Understand the boundary", "Aspire discovers the separate Web API. Validate the trimmed prompt before any model request, and keep credentials only in the API."),
        ("03 / SDK", "Read an async stream", "Use the official Anthropic C# SDK and await foreach to observe text deltas, usage and the final stop reason."),
        ("04 / RESULT", "Separate progress from completion", "Intermediate text is progress. Only a completed message becomes a final result; early limits remain visible."),
        ("05 / PRESENTATION", "Make the answer readable", "Sanitized Markdown, colored code, generous typography and pastel cards support a clear learning experience."),
        ("06 / ARCHITECTURE", "Trace the entire journey", "Inspect Aspire resources and telemetry, then match all 16 UML arrows to real source excerpts and live public events.")];
    private static readonly (string Label, string Title, string Text)[] Layers = [
        ("01 / UI", "MAUI / Razor", "Shared prompt, mode, typed state and timeline."),
        ("02 / HTTP", "ASP.NET Core", "Validation, configuration and SSE framing."),
        ("03 / SDK", "Anthropic C# SDK", "CreateStreaming and async iteration."),
        ("04 / MODEL", "Claude API", "Inference, text deltas and token usage.")];
}
